course: dictionary
lesson: 14883
title: Reciprocal: given and received in return
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reciprocal means that something goes both ways. Each person gives, and each person gets something back. «Their friendship was reciprocal: Sam helped Maya with reading, and Maya helped Sam with drawing.» Both children did something for the other, so the friendship is reciprocal.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Words like «each other», «both» and «in return» often show that something is reciprocal. «The two schools made a reciprocal arrangement: each one hosts the other's sports day.» Try your meaning in the sentence: "an arrangement that goes both ways" still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: In maths, reciprocal is a special word for numbers. The reciprocal of a number is 1 divided by that number. «The reciprocal of 4 is 1/4.» Check it: 4 times 1/4 equals 1, so the answer is correct.
fact: Reciprocal means given and received in return, or done by both people or sides for each other.
fact: Reciprocal is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «reciprocal respect».
fact: «Reciprocal respect» means both people show respect to each other.
fact: In maths, the reciprocal of a number is 1 divided by that number.
fact: A number times its reciprocal equals 1, as in «2 × 1/2 = 1».
exercise: «Ben helped Ali with maths, and Ali helped Ben with spelling. Their help was reciprocal.» What does reciprocal mean here? | Very loud | *Given and received in return by both | Given by only one person | Forgotten quickly
exercise: What is the reciprocal of 5? | 15 | *1/5 | 5 | 0
exercise: What is the reciprocal of 1/3? | *3 | 0 | 1/9 | 1/3
test: «The two countries made a reciprocal agreement to share their science research.» What does reciprocal mean in this sentence? | *Both sides give and get something back | Only one side helps | Signed in ink | Very long
test: Multiply 6 by its reciprocal. What do you get? | 0 | 1/6 | *1 | 6
exam: Which example shows reciprocal respect? | Only the teacher listens to the class | *Each friend listens to the other and values their ideas | Nobody speaks at all | One student shouts while the other sleeps
